# Claude Code (Issue #134)
# settings.local.json is per-developer (permission allowlist etc.) - the
# "local" in the name is the convention signal that it's not meant to be
# shared. It was tracked by mistake, which is why it kept showing up
# modified-but-unstaged every session; untracked via git rm --cached in the
# same commit that added this line.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Skill content materialized from skills-lock.json (source: GitHub repos,
# tracked via computedHash) - regenerable, analogous to node_modules/ from
# package-lock.json. The lock files themselves ARE committed.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
backend/.agents/
